<spell-notebook "search theming">
	<header level="1">
		Search
		<header>A search module allows a user to query for results from a selection of data.</>
	</>
	<search-tab-bar showing="theming"/>
	<section>
		<html>
			<ui-menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
				<ui-item link="#tokens">Tokens</>
				<ui-item link="#themes">Themes</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- THEMING:  the family's tokens, live, plus how to set them and which themes touch it. -->
	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			Theme with the public `--ui-search-*` tokens: set one on the element, on any ancestor (`:root` included), or on
			one piece through `::part(input)` / `::part(results)`. They inherit into the shadow root, where the sheet reads
			each through a private alias, so nothing inside blocks them. `prompt` is the text field itself.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```css
			/* every search on the page:  square-ish prompts */
			:root {
			  --ui-search-prompt-radius: var(--ui-radius);
			}
			/* one search's results, wider */
			ui-search.site-search::part(results) {
			  --ui-search-results-width: 24em;
			}
			```
		</>
		<message state="info" size="small">
			<markdown>
				`--ui-search-results-max-height` replaces the viewport-based height of `scrolling` results at every width;
				`length` (`very-short`, `long` and `very-long`) scales whatever it is (0.75x, 2x, 3x). `category` results use the
				`--ui-search-category-*` tokens. Never set the `--_ui-*` / `--_search-*` names: they're the sheet's private
				plumbing.
			</>
		</>
		<markdown>Edit a value below to try it.</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-search" playground>
				<ui-search placeholder="Common passwords..." source="\[{\"title\":\"123456\"},{\"title\":\"password\"},{\"title\":\"qwerty\"},{\"title\":\"letmein\"},{\"title\":\"dragon\"}]"></>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>
			The theme menu in the header (Spell, Glass, Fruity, Merlot, Paper, Midnight, Crisp, Pop, Matrix) changes the colours, radii and fonts a
			search inherits.
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
